Q. What are Pure & Impure functions in JS ?
    Answer:

        1. Pure function
        --------------------
            function add(a,b){
                return a+b;
            }

            console.log(add(3,5));
            console.log(add(3,5));

        -> A pure function is a function that always produces the same output for the same input.
        -> A pure cannot modify state.
        -> An pure function cannot have side effects.

        2. Impure function
        -----------------------------
            let total = 0;

            function addTotal(value){
                total += value;
                return total;
            }

            console.log(addTotal(5));

        -> An impure function, can produce different outputs for the same input.
        -> An impure function cannot modify state.
        -> An impure function can have side effects.

