Q. What are call, apply and bind methods in JS ?
    Answer:
            const user = {
              name: "Amir"
            };

            function greet(city, country) {
              console.log(
                "Hello " + this.name + " from " + city + ", " + country
              );
            }

        1. call()
            -> Function turant call hota hai
            -> Arguments comma separated

            greet.call(user, "Delhi", "India");
            //output: Hello Amir from Delhi, India

        2. apply()
            -> Function turant call hota hai
            -> Arguments array ke andar

            greet.apply(user, ["Mumbai", "India"]);
            //output: Hello Amir from Mumbai, India

